Day -8(React js)

        Introduction :
                react is one of the most popular java script language used for moders websites and for web applications
        what is react js? 
                react ia a js library used to create user interface
        who is developed the react just
                meta facebook
        key fetures
                component based archicture 
                virtual term 
                reusable code 
                fast performance
        why react js popular
                because it makes web applications posters and reusable peice of using
        uderstanding jsx 
                framework will built using the html
        why should we use react
                before react supose we need to update one button using normal java script  
                finds element, changes content, Update data
                this becomes diffucult in large projects
                react js is solved, reusable components, faster rendering, easy maintance, better user experience
        react js archicture
                react applications is divided into small reusable components 
                EX : head of the app 
                header          ex: search bar
                side bar        ex: menu
                content         ex: content in the app
                footer          ex: below details
        setting up react js project
                1: instatll node js check version
                2: create react app 
                3: moving into the project or enter into the folder
                4: start applications
        what is jsx
                java script xml
                it allowes us to erite the html like code inside the javascript
        jsx syntax rules
                single parent element   
                        ex: return(
                                <h1>Hello</h1>
                                <p>Welcome</p>
                        )

                        ex: return(
                        <div>
                        <h1>hello</h1>
                        <p>welcome</p>
                        </div>)
